            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>Applicable Scenarios and Prerequisites</h2>
<p>This guide applies to operations teams managing multiple overseas advertising accounts (Meta, Google, TikTok for Business, etc.), especially for projects with daily spend exceeding $1,000. If your team frequently encounters the following issues, we recommend reviewing the SOP step by step:</p>
<ul>
<li>Account balance running low causing ads to pause unexpectedly</li>
<li>Payment processing delays affecting campaign scheduling</li>
<li>Discrepancies between spend data and invoices during financial reconciliation</li>
<li>Scattered funds across multiple accounts, making coordination difficult</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 1: Build a Fund Monitoring Dashboard</h2>
<p>Operations staff should check real-time balances and daily spend projections for all accounts at the start of each business day. We recommend maintaining these fields in a spreadsheet:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Account</th>
<th>Platform</th>
<th>Yesterday Balance</th>
<th>Yesterday Spend</th>
<th>Today's Projection</th>
<th>Alert Threshold</th>
<th>Status</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Account A</td>
<td>Meta</td>
<td>$3,200</td>
<td>$800</td>
<td>$850</td>
<td>$1,500</td>
<td>Normal</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Account B</td>
<td>TikTok</td>
<td>$950</td>
<td>$420</td>
<td>$400</td>
<td>$1,000</td>
<td>Alert</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Operational Key Points</strong>:</p>
<ol>
<li>Complete the first check before 9:00 AM (Beijing Time)</li>
<li>Add a review during peak spending hours (overseas evening)</li>
<li>Alert threshold recommended at 2-3x the account's daily average spend</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>Step 2: Set Up Balance Alert Mechanisms</h2>
<p>When account balance falls below the alert threshold, the system or responsible person needs to respond within 30 minutes. Here's the tiered response strategy:</p>
<p><strong>Yellow Alert (Balance at 1-2x daily spend)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Assess if today's remaining budget is sufficient</li>
<li>Notify finance to prepare for recharge</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Red Alert (Balance insufficient for today's spend)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Immediately contact Yiyu Digital Media's customer service or account manager for recharge application</li>
<li>Confirm recharge arrival time and estimate ad interruption duration</li>
<li>If interruption is unavoidable, coordinate with campaign managers to reduce budget or pause low-performing ad groups</li>
</ul>
<p>A utility app team once lost approximately $2,300 in potential conversions due to a 4-hour interruption at 2 AM during peak season promotion, caused by lack of alert settings. Such issues are entirely preventable through SOP implementation.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 3: Develop Recharge Plans and Priorities</h2>
<p>Operations teams should create weekly recharge schedules based on account importance and spending velocity:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Every Monday</strong>: Compile weekly spend projections for all accounts</li>
<li><strong>Every Tuesday</strong>: Submit recharge applications with priority markers</li>
<li><strong>Recharge Confirmation</strong>: Update balance in monitoring table immediately upon arrival</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Priority Criteria</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>Number of active ad groups (higher count = higher priority)</li>
<li>Remaining Days = Balance ÷ Daily Average Spend (recharge immediately if under 2 days)</li>
<li>Campaign lifecycle stage (testing period takes priority over stable scaling period)</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 4: Optimize Spending Rhythm</h2>
<p>Fund management isn't just about "ensuring money is available"—it's about aligning spending rhythm with campaign objectives.</p>
<p><strong>Core Metrics Quick Reference</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Daily Spend Variance Rate</strong> = (Actual Spend - Planned Spend) ÷ Planned Spend × 100%</li>
<li>Acceptable range: within ±15%</li>
<li><strong>Fund Utilization Rate</strong> = Conversion Value from Ads ÷ Total Spend × 100%</li>
<li>Pause underperforming campaigns if below baseline</li>
<li><strong>Payback Cycle Coverage</strong> = Account Balance ÷ Daily Average Spend</li>
<li>Ensure coverage of payment cycle to avoid cash flow pressure</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Practical Recommendations</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>Set spending cap at 50% of budget for the first 3 days when launching new accounts, then gradually increase after observing stability</li>
<li>When reallocating budget across multiple accounts, prioritize accounts with the highest ROAS</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 5: Financial Reconciliation and Risk Control</h2>
<p><strong>Weekly Reconciliation Process</strong>:</p>
<ol>
<li>Download statements from each platform (typically 1-3 days delayed)</li>
<li>Cross-check against recharge records and spend records</li>
<li>When discrepancies exceed 2%, screenshot and archive, then verify with platform or agency</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Common Discrepancy Reasons</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>Time zone differences affecting spend statistics calculation</li>
<li>Refunds or credits not updated promptly</li>
<li>Account-to-account balance transfers not recorded separately</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Risk Control Red Lines</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>Multiple recharge applications for the same account from the same IP within 1 minute (may trigger risk controls)</li>
<li>Account balance consistently at zero (affects future appeal success rate)</li>
<li>Recharge card holder different from account registration entity (strictly restricted on some platforms)</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Quick Checklist</h2>
<p>Operations staff can quickly review at the end of each workday:</p>
<ul>
<li>[ ] All active account balances are above alert thresholds</li>
<li>[ ] Submitted recharges have confirmed arrival</li>
<li>[ ] Tomorrow's spend projections are updated</li>
<li>[ ] Abnormal spend is marked and root cause investigated</li>
<li>[ ] Financial reconciliation records are archived</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Conclusion</h2>
<p>The essence of overseas advertising fund management is finding balance between "ensuring delivery continuity" and "controlling idle capital costs." Operations teams don't need to become finance experts, but they must master these 5 steps and adjust thresholds based on their actual spending scale in practice.</p>
